# Rational Economics in Comparison to the Case of Behavioral Economics (Keynesian, and Neoclassical Approaches)

**Authors:** Constantinos Challoumis Κωνσταντίνος Χαλλουμής

## Abstract
This paper aims to represent the special characteristics of rational economics in comparison to the case of the behavioral economics. Therefore, in this analysis are represented these issues, and showed the main differences between the two concepts. Therefore, the mainstream is to show the crucial attributes for both of them, and differences between them.

